            <ArticleTitle>Towards painless orthopaedic surgery.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>146-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Almost one thousand patients underwent either total hip replacement or spinal surgery in which diamorphine 0.5-1.0 mg was injected intrathecally. Approximately one half of the arthroplasty patients and one third of the spinal patients required no other post-operative analgesia. In the remainder, analgesics were not required for 12 hours post-operatively. The benefits of the technique and possible complications are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
